  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 100 AM CST CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nMonday through Saturday:\n\nAnother low pressure system tracking east into Ontario Canada on \nMonday will work with high pressure across the Lower Mississippi\nRiver Valley to drive breezy southwest winds on Monday, with highs\nin the mid to upper 50s. A weak cold front follows Monday night, \nwith light northwest winds and slightly warmer (around 60) high \ntemperatures for Tuesday. \n\nInto Wednesday, high pressure slides southeast across Manitoba and\na deepening trough in the jet dives from the Dakotas towards the\nOhio River Valley. Low pressure develops near the southern tip of\nIL in response to the trough, with both features tracking east. QG\nascent from the approaching trough coupled with some Lake Superior\nboundary layer moisture could result in some light rain Wednesday\n(15-30% chance). Highs in the low 50s.\n\nAs both pressure systems intensify and the low exits east, north\nwinds become gusty across the lake Wednesday night into Thursday.\nLake effect showers will become possible across far eastern WI at\ntimes Wednesday night through Friday. High temperatures dive to\nthe 40s, with lows in the upper 20s to 30s. \n\nSheppard",
